       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day. That is almost four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for adults. A single 5 g dose is also above the normal single-dose limit of 1 g, and this dose would risk severe hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nIt may be a typo. Here are some common intended regimens:\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 5,000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still want to flag it for pharmacist review before entering it."
